        <mxCell id="n27" value="" style="endArrow=block;endFill=1;html=1;strokeColor=#333333;fontSize=11;exitX=1;exitY=0.5;exitDx=0;exitDy=0;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;entryDx=0;entryDy=0;" edge="1" parent="1" source="n11" target="n18"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="n28" value="" style="endArrow=block;endFill=1;html=1;strokeColor=#333333;fontSize=11;exitX=0;exitY=0.5;exitDx=0;exitDy=0;entryX=1;entryY=0.5;entryDx=0;entryDy=0;" edge="1" parent="1" source="n18" target="n6"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"><Array as="points"><mxPoint x="1300" y="455"/><mxPoint x="1300" y="537"/></Array></mxGeometry></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="n29" value="" style="endArrow=block;endFill=1;html=1;strokeColor=#333333;fontSize=11;exitX=1;exitY=0.5;exitDx=0;exitDy=0;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;entryDx=0;entryDy=0;" edge="1" parent="1" source="n6" target="n19"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="n30" value="" style="endArrow=block;endFill=1;html=1;strokeColor=#333333;fontSize=11;" edge="1" parent="1" source="n19" target="n20"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="n31" value="" style="endArrow=block;endFill=1;html=1;strokeColor=#333333;fontSize=11;exitX=0;exitY=0.5;exitDx=0;exitDy=0;entryX=1;entryY=0.5;entryDx=0;entryDy=0;" edge="1" parent="1" source="n20" target="n13"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="n32" value="" style="endArrow=block;endFill=1;html=1;strokeColor=#333333;fontSize=11;" edge="1" parent="1" source="n13" target="n14"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="n33" value="yes" style="endArrow=block;endFill=1;html=1;strokeColor=#333333;fontSize=11;exitX=1;exitY=0.5;exitDx=0;exitDy=0;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;entryDx=0;entryDy=0;" edge="1" parent="1" source="n14" target="n15"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="n34" value="no" style="endArrow=block;endFill=1;html=1;strokeColor=#333333;fontSize=11;" edge="1" parent="1" source="n14" target="n16"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="n35" value="COMMIT" style="endArrow=block;endFill=1;html=1;strokeColor=#333333;fontSize=11;" edge="1" parent="1" source="n16" target="n17"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="n36" value="THE HOLE THAT WAS HERE UNTIL 14 AUGUST&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;POST /api/v1/payments with body {&quot;amount&quot;: 999999999} called&lt;br&gt;walletsService.topup(user.id, amount) directly. Any signed-in account could&lt;br&gt;credit itself any sum. No bank transfer, no admin, no PayOS — and the ledger&lt;br&gt;entry it produced was indistinguishable from a real top-up.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;The money was immediately spendable, and withdrawable through&lt;br&gt;POST /withdrawals. Only the admin approval step stood between a fabricated&lt;br&gt;balance and a real bank payout — and the admin sees nothing but a normal&lt;br&gt;looking balance.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;POST /wallets/topup was worse in a quieter way: WalletsController carried no&lt;br&gt;guard at all, so a route into a function that writes to the ledger was&lt;br&gt;reachable without logging in. It answered 500 rather than 401 only because&lt;br&gt;@User() returned undefined and the code tripped over user.id.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Fixed: the /payments branch refuses and names the PayOS route; the wallets&lt;br&gt;controller takes JwtAuthGuard at class level and AdminGuard on topup;&lt;br&gt;route-guards.spec.ts now fails the build if any route loses its guard." style="shape=note;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;size=14;verticalAlign=top;align=left;spacingLeft=6;fontSize=11;fillColor=#fffbe6;strokeColor=#c8a415;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="40" y="1190" width="840" height="330" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="n37" value="Why the wallet is only credited by the webhook&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;The ledger account `gateway_clearing` represents money that PayOS is holding&lt;br&gt;on our behalf. Every credit to a user wallet is paid for out of it, so the sum&lt;br&gt;of what we have handed out must always match what the gateway actually&lt;br&gt;received. Crediting a wallet without a matching bank event breaks that&lt;br&gt;equality, and it breaks it invisibly — the books still balance to zero because&lt;br&gt;the fake entry has two sides. It only surfaces when someone compares&lt;br&gt;gateway_clearing against the PayOS statement.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;That is the whole reason the credit lives in the webhook and nowhere else.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;The idempotency key is payos:{orderCode}:{paymentLinkId}, so PayOS may call&lt;br&gt;the webhook as many times as it likes. The second call finds the transaction&lt;br&gt;already posted and stops — a flow final, not an activity final: the request&lt;br&gt;still returns 200, which is what stops PayOS retrying forever.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;The same key is used by GET /payos/refresh/:orderId, so whichever arrives&lt;br&gt;first wins and the other becomes a no-op." style="shape=note;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;size=14;verticalAlign=top;align=left;spacingLeft=6;fontSize=11;fillColor=#fffbe6;strokeColor=#c8a415;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="910" y="1190" width="840" height="330" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>
</mxfile>
